-- Zone-cell masks (generated by tools/zonemasks/gen_manifest.js from the manifest of tools/zonemasks/partition.js).
-- Each mask is a 256x256 TGA (alpha = the zone's cell) stretched over the zone's whole 1002x668
-- base layer. The cells of a continent tile it: every place belongs to exactly one zone or city.
-- rc = zone rect on its continent {x0, x1, y0, y1} and art = UiMapArtID the mask was made for
-- (WoW Forever 1.60.1.70009); Render.lua only uses a mask while both still match the client.
-- nz = layer-px box {x0, y0, x1, y1} outside which the mask is zero.
-- (1.0.1) Every ZONE mask also takes the open sea (and odd strips at the map edges) no cell covers whose
-- nearest land is that zone's, fading out with distance from that land and softly towards its picture's frame,
-- crossfading into a neighbour's (tools/history/v3.2.0/apply320.py): its cell draws them from the zone's sharp art.
-- (1.2.0) A capital whose map holds land no cell covers (Orgrimmar, Stormwind) also has patch / pcover / pnz: its
-- patch mask (Render.lua BuildCityLod, the city above the switch: its cell and that land, inside the printed frame;
-- the emblems printed there carved out), the whole patch for their copies (ns.CityPatchCovers), and the patch's
-- nonzero box.
